> You can only wish for objects (so 'no hunger' will not work that way).
>
> You cannot ask for many objects (if you ask for more than one, there are
> risks that you will only get one, the bigger the number you ask, the
> higher the risk).
>
> (so you could ask for 2 or 3 food rations, and get them, but that will not
> keep your hunger at bay for a really long time, there are better things to
> wish for (especially since there are plenty of other stuff to eat in that
> dungeon...))
>
> But you can ask for (almost) any object in the game, even the more
> powerful ones. [not the Amulet of Yendor or similar object, and not a wand
> of wishing or similar objects]
>
>
> When you ask for something, specify *everything* you want. It is always
> frustrating to ask for "a sword" and get "a cursed -5 short sword" [did it
> in the beginning...] so, among other, ask specifially for "a blessed"
> something (you should probably not need unblessed stuff right now), and
> specify an enchantment for weapons and armors (again, a too high
> anchantment can result in a +0, similarly as asking for many items).
>
>
> After that, the point is to now what will be the most powerfull stuff
> you'll need right now...
>
> Since you're a samurai, you probably need either weapon or armor (rather
> than, eg spellbook).
>
> I guess, you've already come across some good armor such as mithril ones,
> so you may try (with few spoiler) asking for "a blessed +2 dwarvish
> mithril coat", but that is a bit wasted since you can often find them in
> the mines.
>
> You can also ask for rings which are a bit less common. Among other and
> for the most useful, you may want slow digestion, regeneration [obvious
> use], free action or conflict [less obvious use but really useful too].
